  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Love Language Quiz FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a love language quiz?\", \"a\": \"A love language quiz is a short set of questions that shows which love language a person's answers favor, such as Quality Time or Acts of Service. The idea comes from a 1992 nonfiction book by Baptist pastor Gary Chapman, which outlines five general ways that romantic partners express and experience love.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a love language quiz?\", \"a\": \"Describe the quiz in a prompt, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> writes the questions, a result screen for each language, and the table that saves every result. Ask for a follow-up in the same prompt or a later one, such as an email to you when someone finishes. Then share the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should each result in a 5 love languages quiz tell the person?\", \"a\": \"It should name the leading language and show what it looks like in a normal week. Chapman's book includes questions to help readers identify both their own and their partner's primary and secondary love languages. Show the runner-up too. Close with two small things to try, like a phone-free dinner for Quality Time.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I offer a free love language quiz on my own website?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing. Keep the result screen free of sign-up walls. The setup behind it, where each option points to one result, is the same one that runs a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should my free 5 love languages quiz ask for an email before the result?\", \"a\": \"No, show the result first. A visitor asked for an email before seeing anything has no reason to trust the quiz yet. Put an optional email field under the result, with a plain reason to give it, such as two ideas a week for their language. On Emergent, every address lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a five love languages quiz have?\", \"a\": \"Eight is a good number. With one option per language in each question, 8 questions give every language 8 chances to come out ahead, and a person on a phone can finish in one sitting. Past 10, the questions start to sound alike. The quiz on this page uses 8.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a love language quiz decide which result to show?\", \"a\": \"It counts. Each option points to one language, and the language picked most often becomes the result. No answer is right or wrong, unlike a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a>, which scores answers against a key. Decide ahead of time how a tie breaks, for example by showing both languages.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where do the five results in a love language quiz come from?\", \"a\": \"They come from The Five Love Languages, a 1992 nonfiction book by Gary Chapman. He theorizes that people tend to naturally give love in the way that they prefer to receive love. That is why a good quiz asks both how someone likes to be cared for and how they show care.\"}, {\"q\": \"How accurate are love language quiz results?\", \"a\": \"Treat them as a starting point. Scientific studies on the validity of love languages have yielded mixed or inconclusive results, and a 2023 review found that existing research does not confirm that individuals reliably have a preferred love language. Say so in one line on the result screen, and frame each result as a leaning.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a coach use a love language quiz to find new clients?\", \"a\": \"Put the quiz where prospects already read, like a newsletter or podcast show notes, and end each result with one offer. If the offer is a free first session, send that click to a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a> that explains the session and books it. The app records which result each new client came from, in a database you own.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
